  "why": "These classes were added to src/client/styles.css BEFORE any page wears them, so that five tab branches start from one rule set. validate:css-classes proves every className used has a rule; it cannot see a rule nobody uses. This register is the other direction: every class here must have a rule now, must be emitted once every tab that owns it has landed, and a tab is marked landed the moment anything emits one of its classes. Read by scripts/validate/css-classes.mjs and scripts/validate/heading-scale-applies.mjs; a tab agent flips its `landed` flag in the PR that emits the classes, and edits `owners` when the page it built does not use a class the spec named for it.",
